# OPTIONAL - delete this file to undo it. Nothing else changes.
#
# The mod already had a Cobra front company before the economy existed:
# STR_COBRA_FRONT in gijoe_frontops.rul, with its own warehouse terrain and
# its own briefing about the Crimson Twins moving money under a legitimate
# name. The economy then added a second front company that does not know
# about the first.
#
# So over eleven months of a test campaign Cobra put eight of the old fronts
# on the globe and earned nothing from any of them, while the economy's own
# front company sat alone and could afford almost nothing. The intel screen
# reported three sites while the globe showed twenty-three.
#
# This one line tells the economy that the front company it already had IS a
# front company. It loads after gijoe_frontops.rul and merges into the same
# deployment, so John's file is untouched and removing this file puts
# everything back.
#
# WHAT IT DOES TO THE PACE, measured over the same eleven months:
#
#   neither file          3 sites    front company, depot, training camp
#   this file alone      14 sites    but NINE OF THEM OUTSIDE NORTH AMERICA
#   both files           12 sites    all North America, five of the eight
#                                    types built and still wanting more
#
# THE MIDDLE ROW IS WHY zz_gijoe_frontops_region.rul EXISTS. Your front-op
# scripts name no region, so they put fronts anywhere on the globe - which
# was harmless while they were scenery and is not harmless the moment they
# are earners, because only North America has G.I. Joe terrain. I shipped
# this file on its own first and only found that by running the campaign and
# printing the region of every site. Use the two together.
#
# The swing is still large and it is a balance question, not a bug fix,
# which is why both are files you can delete rather than something baked in.

alienDeployments:
  - type: STR_COBRA_FRONT
    cobraSiteType: STR_COBRA_FRONT_COMPANY
